  "id": "Compound::DB00526 - Gene::538",
  "verbalization": "Oxaliplatin, a platinum-containing compound, is linked to Atp7a through a series of molecular interactions that involve the transport of copper ions. The evidence suggests that Oxaliplatin, as part of the broader class of platinum-containing compounds, binds to and influences the activity of Slc31a1, which is involved in copper ion transmembrane transport. This interaction ultimately leads to Atp7a being engaged in copper transport processes. The shared pathway through Platinum Compound and Platinum Coordination Entity indicates a common mechanism by which Oxaliplatin affects Atp7a, likely through the modulation of copper ion transport. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Oxaliplatin in modulating copper homeostasis, which may underlie its biological effects. The evidence supports a mechanism where Oxaliplatin indirectly influences Atp7a via Slc31a1, emphasizing the importance of copper transport in the cellular response to platinum-based chemotherapy.",
